LONG.update({
'start-album-design-business':('How to Start an Album Design Service from Home',[
"Many photographers outsource album design, especially during the wedding season, which creates steady work for skilled designers who work from home. If you are comfortable with Photoshop and enjoy layout work, an album design service can be built with modest equipment. This guide covers the practical steps; it does not promise any particular income, because that depends on your skills, speed and clients.",
"## Skills you need",
"- Confident Photoshop use: layers, clipping masks, adjustment layers, selections and actions.",
"- Layout sense: hierarchy, alignment, spacing and consistency across an album.",
"- Colour correction: matching skin tones and lighting across many photos.",
"- Print knowledge: sizes, DPI, bleed, colour profiles and lab requirements.",
"- Communication: understanding a studio's style and handling revisions calmly.",
"Our guides on [editing a wedding album PSD](/blog/how-to-edit-wedding-album-psd/), [layout rules](/blog/wedding-album-layout-rules/) and the [print-ready checklist](/blog/print-ready-psd-checklist/) are a good self-check.",
"## Equipment",
"A computer that handles large PSDs comfortably (16 GB RAM or more, an SSD), a monitor you can calibrate, a hardware calibrator if possible, reliable internet for large uploads and downloads, and backup storage. A licensed copy of Photoshop is essential for professional work.",
"## Build a portfolio",
"Studios hire based on samples. Design a set of sample spreads in different styles: traditional, royal, minimal, pre-wedding and birthday. If you do not yet have client photos, ask photographer friends for permission to use a few images, or use photos you have rights to. Show complete spreads, not single frames, and include before-and-after colour correction examples.",
"## Decide your service and pricing model",
"Common models are per sheet, per album or a monthly retainer for regular studios. Define clearly what is included: number of revision rounds, colour correction, cover design and delivery format. Research what designers in your region charge by talking to studios and other designers, then price based on your time and experience rather than undercutting everyone.",
"## Find clients",
"- Local studios and photographers, especially those who shoot many weddings.",
"- Album printing labs, which often know photographers who need designers.",
"- Photographer communities and groups on social media, following their rules.",
"- Referrals from satisfied clients; ask for them.",
"See our guide on [getting album design freelance work](/blog/album-design-freelance-guide/) for outreach tips.",
"## Set up a reliable workflow",
"- A standard intake form: album size, sheet count, lab, style, must-include photos, names and dates.",
"- A folder structure for every project.",
"- A preview process for client approval, such as a PDF of all spreads.",
"- Clear file naming and delivery to the lab or studio.",
"## Use templates wisely",
"Templates speed up work, but studios pay for your judgement and consistency. Build your own library of layouts adapted from free templates such as our [Karizma album PSD collection](/karizma-album-psd/), which can be used for client work, and keep developing a recognisable style.",
"## Legal and practical basics",
"Use licensed software and fonts, respect clients' photo privacy and do not share client images without permission. Keep simple written agreements covering deliverables, revisions, payment terms and turnaround. Keep records of income and expenses and check tax registration requirements that apply to you.",
"## Grow steadily",
"Start with a few regular studios, deliver on time and keep quality consistent. Reliability is what brings repeat work during the busy season."]),
'does-photoshop-have-album-templates':('Does Photoshop Have Album Templates? Where to Find Them',[
"New album designers often look for an 'album template' option inside Photoshop. Photoshop does include some document presets and access to Adobe Stock templates, but it does not come with a ready library of Indian-style wedding album sheets such as 12x36 Karizma layouts. Most designers use PSD templates from other sources or build their own.",
"## What Photoshop includes",
"When you create a new document (File > New), Photoshop shows presets for common print and screen sizes and a selection of templates, many from Adobe Stock. Some are free and some require a licence. These templates tend to be general-purpose: social media posts, flyers, photo collages and mockups. They rarely match Indian album sizes and styles, so you will still need to adapt them.",
"## Setting up your own album canvas",
"You can create a blank album canvas in a few seconds:",
"- File > New, set the width and height in inches (for example 36 x 12 for a 12x36 spread).",
"- Set the resolution, typically 300 or 200 pixels per inch, as your lab requires.",
"- Choose RGB colour, 8-bit, and the sRGB profile.",
"- Save it as a preset so it appears in the New Document dialog next time.",
"Then add guides for the centre fold (18 inches on a 36 inch sheet) and safe margins. A blank canvas is useful for custom designs and for adapting layouts.",
"## Where designers get album templates",
"- **Free template sites:** PSD Album offers thousands of free 12x36, 12x30, 18x24 and 12x18 layered sheets with no login, each with a full preview and specs. Start with the [12x36 wedding album PSD collection](/12x36-wedding-album-psd-free-download/) or the [Karizma album PSD collection](/karizma-album-psd/).",
"- **Premium template collections:** paid sites and template packs offer larger, curated libraries.",
"- **Your own library:** many experienced designers save their best adapted layouts as personal templates.",
"## What makes a good album template",
"- Layered, with photo frames as clipping-mask bases.",
"- Built at the correct proportions and resolution for your album size.",
"- Grouped and named layers so you can find frames, text and decorations easily.",
"- Editable text layers for names and dates.",
"- Decorations that can be hidden or recoloured.",
"Avoid flattened JPG 'templates' with transparent holes; they are hard to adapt and often low resolution.",
"## Safety when downloading",
"Download templates from reputable sources. Be cautious with password-protected ZIPs, executable files or sites that require you to install software. A genuine PSD download is a .psd file, usually inside a ZIP; it never needs to be 'run'.",
"## Other software",
"Dedicated album design tools offer automatic layouts and templates, and some designers use them alongside Photoshop. See our comparison of [album design software options](/blog/album-design-software-options/). Even with those tools, Photoshop remains the standard for detailed retouching and custom layouts.",
"## Getting started",
"Download a template, open it in Photoshop and follow [how to edit a wedding album PSD](/blog/how-to-edit-wedding-album-psd/) to place your photos and export for print."]),
'album-design-software-options':('Album Design Software: Photoshop vs Dedicated Album Tools',[
"Studios can design albums in a general-purpose editor like Adobe Photoshop or in dedicated album design software that automates layouts. Each approach has strengths, and many studios use both. This guide compares them so you can choose what fits your workflow. Features and pricing change frequently, so check each vendor's current information before buying.",
"## Adobe Photoshop",
"Photoshop is the industry standard for image editing and detailed layout work.",
"- **Strengths:** complete control over every pixel, advanced retouching and selections, clipping masks for templates, adjustment layers, actions for automation, and compatibility with almost every PSD template.",
"- **Limitations:** no automatic album layout; each spread is a separate document; large albums can be slow on modest computers; requires a subscription.",
"- **Best for:** custom designs, heavy retouching, using PSD template libraries and premium albums where every spread is crafted.",
"## Adobe Lightroom Classic book module",
"Lightroom includes a Book module with layout templates, mainly connected to specific print services. It is convenient if you already organise photos in Lightroom, but it offers less design flexibility than Photoshop and is not tailored to Indian album sizes and lab workflows.",
"## Dedicated album design tools",
"Several commercial applications are built specifically for album design. Typical features include automatic placement of photos into layouts, drag-and-drop spreads, built-in templates, export to lab specifications and client proofing tools.",
"- **Strengths:** very fast for high-volume work, consistent layouts, built-in proofing.",
"- **Limitations:** less control over fine details, template styles may not suit every client, additional licence costs, and you may still need Photoshop for retouching.",
"- **Best for:** studios that produce many albums with similar styles and want speed.",
"## Free alternatives",
"Free editors such as GIMP or browser-based tools like Photopea can open many PSD files and handle basic edits. They can be useful for learning or quick fixes, but clipping masks, smart objects and adjustment layers may behave differently, and large 300 DPI sheets can be slow. See [how to edit a PSD without Photoshop](/blog/edit-psd-without-photoshop/) for details.",
"## A hybrid workflow",
"Many studios combine tools: Lightroom for culling and colour correction, an album tool or templates for fast layout, and Photoshop for final retouching and custom spreads. The key is to keep the colour profile, sizes and file naming consistent across tools.",
"## How to choose",
"- **Volume:** if you design many albums each month, automation can save significant time.",
"- **Style:** if your brand relies on custom, editorial layouts, Photoshop offers more control.",
"- **Budget:** consider subscription and licence costs against time saved.",
"- **Hardware:** large albums need adequate RAM and fast storage whichever tool you use.",
"- **Lab compatibility:** confirm the export formats and sizes your lab accepts.",
"## Templates work with Photoshop",
"Free layered templates such as those in our [wedding album design PSD collection](/wedding-album-design-psd/) work directly in Photoshop. If you mainly use templates, Photoshop plus a good library and a few actions is often all you need. Read [how to speed up your album design workflow](/blog/speed-up-album-design-workflow/) for practical tips."]),
'what-is-dm-album-psd':('What Is a DM Album PSD? Meaning for Album Designers',[
"'DM album PSD' is a term widely used among Indian studios and album designers, especially in search queries and template collections. It usually refers to ready-made album sheet designs in PSD format, mostly at 12x36, where the layout, frames, ornaments and text are already designed and you only need to add your photos.",
"## What the term means in practice",
"There is no single official definition, and people use 'DM' loosely. In most template collections, a DM album PSD is a complete double-page sheet (a spread) with clipping-mask photo frames, background, decorations and editable text, ready to be filled with photos. Some designers interpret DM as 'design master' or 'double mount'; usage varies, so focus on what the file contains rather than the label.",
"## Typical features",
"- 12x36 inch spread, often at 300 DPI (10800 x 3600 pixels) or 200 DPI.",
"- Multiple photo frames as separate layers for clipping.",
"- Decorative elements such as florals, mandalas, gold borders or textures.",
"- Editable text layers for names, dates and event titles.",
"- Background layers that can be recoloured.",
"## How to use a DM album PSD",
"- Check the canvas size and DPI against your lab's requirements.",
"- Open the Layers panel and identify the frame layers.",
"- Place each photo directly above its frame and clip it with Alt+Ctrl+G.",
"- Resize photos with Ctrl+T, keeping faces away from the centre fold.",
"- Edit the text and recolour ornaments with clipped adjustment layers.",
"- Save the layered PSD and export a flattened sRGB JPG for print.",
"Our step-by-step guide on [editing a wedding album PSD](/blog/how-to-edit-wedding-album-psd/) covers each step in detail.",
"## Choosing good DM sheets",
"- Prefer layered files with named, grouped layers.",
"- Check that frames match the orientation of your photos.",
"- Avoid designs with heavy decoration behind faces.",
"- Choose a consistent set for each event in the album.",
"## Watch out for unsafe downloads",
"Many 'DM album PSD free download' posts bundle files behind ZIP passwords, link shorteners or software installers. A legitimate PSD template does not require installing anything. On PSD Album every design has its own page with a full preview and specifications and downloads directly from Google Drive with no password and no login. See the [DM album PSD collection](/dm-album-psd/).",
"## DM sheets vs custom design",
"Ready-made sheets save time and are perfect for consistent, traditional albums. For premium clients who want a unique album, use DM sheets as a starting grid, then customise frames, colours and typography so the final design feels personal.",
"## Building your own library",
"Over time, save your adapted DM sheets as clean templates with empty frames. Organise them by event and frame count. This turns free templates into a personal design system that speeds up every album you make."]),
'album-design-freelance-guide':('How to Get Album Design Freelance Work',[
"Freelance album design can provide regular work, particularly during the wedding season when studios are overloaded. Getting the first few clients is the hardest part. This guide focuses on practical, honest ways to find and keep album design clients.",
"## Prepare before you pitch",
"- **Portfolio:** 10 to 20 complete spreads in different styles: traditional wedding, royal Karizma, minimal pre-wedding, birthday and baby albums. Include a full sample album if you can.",
"- **Process sheet:** a one-page summary of how you work: intake, turnaround, revisions, delivery format and payment terms.",
"- **Pricing:** clear rates per sheet or per album, with what is included.",
"See [how to start an album design service from home](/blog/start-album-design-business/) for setting up equipment and workflow.",
"## Where to find clients",
"- **Local studios:** visit or message photographers who shoot many weddings. Offer a sample spread designed from their own photos (with their permission) to show your style.",
"- **Album labs:** labs interact with many photographers and often know who needs designers. Some labs also hire designers directly.",
"- **Photographer communities:** many groups exist for photographers and album designers. Contribute helpful advice, share work where allowed and avoid spamming.",
"- **Freelance platforms:** general freelance marketplaces have album design requests, though competition on price can be intense.",
"- **Referrals:** ask every satisfied client to recommend you to other photographers.",
"## Make a strong first impression",
"Studios care about three things: quality, consistency and deadlines. Deliver your first project slightly ahead of schedule, follow their instructions exactly and keep communication short and clear. A single reliable season can lead to long-term work.",
"## Handle revisions professionally",
"Agree in advance how many revision rounds are included. Collect all changes in one list per round. Use preview PDFs so studios and their clients can comment easily; see [how to make a wedding album PDF for client approval](/blog/wedding-album-pdf-for-client-approval/).",
"## Protect clients' photos",
"Studios trust you with private family photos. Never post client images publicly without explicit permission, keep files secure and delete or archive them as agreed after the project.",
"## Get paid reliably",
"- Ask for an advance for new clients.",
"- Send invoices with clear descriptions and due dates.",
"- Deliver final print files after payment for new clients; share previews before that.",
"- Keep records of all transactions.",
"## Increase your value",
"- Learn colour correction thoroughly; studios value designers who fix inconsistent photos.",
"- Offer extra services such as cover design, parent albums and invitation design.",
"- Build a template library so you can deliver faster without lowering quality. Free resources like our [wedding album design PSD collection](/wedding-album-design-psd/) can be used for client work.",
"## Plan for the seasons",
"Wedding seasons create peaks and quieter periods. Use quiet months to build your portfolio, learn new techniques and reach out to new studios, so your calendar fills before the next peak."]),
'how-to-fix-zip-extraction-errors':('How to Fix ZIP Extraction Errors When Downloading PSDs',[
"Large PSD templates are usually delivered as ZIP files, and a few hundred megabytes is common for 300 DPI album sheets. If extraction fails or the PSD will not open, the cause is almost always an incomplete download or a tool that struggles with large files. This guide explains how to fix the common errors.",
"## Error: 'The archive is corrupt' or 'Unexpected end of archive'",
"This means the file did not download completely. Check the file size on your computer against the size listed on the design page. If yours is smaller, download again. Tips for large downloads:",
"- Use a stable Wi-Fi or wired connection rather than mobile data.",
"- Use a desktop browser such as Chrome, Edge or Firefox.",
"- Avoid pausing and resuming, and do not close the tab until the download finishes.",
"- Make sure your drive has enough free space for both the ZIP and the extracted file.",
"## Error: 'Windows cannot complete the extraction'",
"The built-in Windows extractor sometimes fails on very large archives or long file paths. Try the following:",
"- Install a well-known free archiver such as 7-Zip and right-click the ZIP > 7-Zip > Extract Here.",
"- Move the ZIP to a short path such as C:\\PSD before extracting, to avoid path length problems.",
"- Rename the ZIP to a short name without special characters.",
"## Error on Mac: 'Unable to expand'",
"Archive Utility occasionally fails with large ZIPs. Use The Unarchiver from the Mac App Store, or open Terminal and run the unzip command on the file. Also confirm the download completed fully.",
"## Error: Password requested",
"PSD Album files do not use passwords. If a ZIP asks for one, it came from another source or the download was redirected. Download again from the design page on psdalbum.in.",
"## The PSD opens but looks wrong",
"- **Missing fonts:** Photoshop shows a warning and substitutes fonts. Replace them with similar fonts you own.",
"- **Very slow:** large sheets need RAM. Close other programs, increase Photoshop's memory in Preferences > Performance and use an SSD as the scratch disk.",
"- **'Not a valid Photoshop document':** usually an incomplete extraction; extract again with 7-Zip.",
"- **Opens in another app:** right-click the PSD > Open with > Adobe Photoshop.",
"## Google Drive messages",
"Google cannot virus-scan very large files, so Drive shows a warning; choose 'Download anyway'. If Drive says the file has been downloaded too many times, wait a few hours and try again, or add it to your own Drive and download from there. Our guide on [how to download PSD files](/blog/how-to-download-psd-files/) explains these steps.",
"## Phones and tablets",
"Large PSD ZIPs are difficult to handle on phones. Download on a computer where you have Photoshop installed. If you must use a phone, use a file manager that supports ZIP extraction and transfer the PSD to your computer.",
"## Still not working?",
"Email contact@psdalbum.in with the design ID (shown as #psd-1234 on the design page), your operating system and the exact error message. We check and fix broken files quickly. Meanwhile, you can browse similar designs in the [12x36 wedding album collection](/12x36-wedding-album-psd-free-download/)."]),
'using-ai-in-album-design':('Using AI Tools in Album Design: What Works Today',[
"AI features are now built into tools that album designers already use, and new ones appear frequently. Some genuinely save time; others are better avoided for client albums. This guide looks at practical uses of AI in album work as of today. Features change quickly, so check the current documentation of the tools you use.",
"## Selections and masking",
"Photoshop's Select Subject, Object Selection and Remove Background features use machine learning to separate people from backgrounds. They are a large time saver for background replacement and studio prints. Always refine edges, especially hair, with Select and Mask, and check the result at 100 percent zoom. See [changing a studio background in Photoshop](/blog/how-to-change-studio-background-in-photoshop/).",
"## Removing distractions",
"Content-aware tools and generative fill can remove small distractions such as a stray cable, an exit sign or a passer-by. They work best on simple backgrounds. Check carefully for repeated patterns, warped lines and odd textures, which can be very visible in print. Be cautious with generative tools on faces and hands, and avoid changing the meaning of a real moment.",
"## Culling and selection",
"Some culling software uses AI to group similar shots and flag closed eyes or missed focus. This can speed up the first pass through thousands of photos, but final selection should still be done by a person who understands the story and the family's priorities.",
"## Colour correction",
"AI-assisted auto adjustments and presets can give a good starting point for exposure and white balance. Skin tones still need careful human review, especially for Indian weddings with mixed lighting. Apply corrections per lighting group and review results before export. Our [colour correction tips](/blog/album-colour-correction-tips/) apply regardless of the tool.",
"## Automatic layouts",
"Dedicated album software can propose layouts automatically. Treat these as drafts: review each spread for the focal point, the centre fold and frame orientation. See [album design software options](/blog/album-design-software-options/).",
"## Upscaling",
"AI upscaling can enlarge a small photo more cleanly than traditional resizing. It can help when a client supplies a low-resolution family photo that must appear in the album. However, it can invent details, especially in faces and text. Use it for small or supporting frames, and compare against the original before printing.",
"## Generating backgrounds and decorations",
"Generative tools can create textures and backgrounds. Check the tool's licence terms for commercial use, avoid generating images that imitate recognisable artwork or trademarks, and make sure results are high enough resolution for print. Free, layered backgrounds such as our [album background PSD collection](/album-background-psd/) remain a predictable option.",
"## Ethics and client trust",
"- Do not alter what happened at an event in a way that misleads; removing a distraction is different from adding people or changing expressions.",
"- Be transparent with clients if generative edits were used in a significant way.",
"- Respect privacy; do not upload client photos to online AI services without understanding how data is stored and used.",
"## A sensible approach",
"Use AI where it removes repetitive work, such as selections, first-pass culling and simple clean-up, and keep human judgement for selection, layout, colour and storytelling. The album is a record of real moments; AI should help you present them, not replace them."]),
'wedding-album-colour-themes':('Choosing a Colour Theme for a Wedding Album',[
"A consistent colour theme is one of the simplest ways to make an album look designed rather than assembled. When backgrounds, ornaments and text share a small palette that matches the photos, every spread feels connected. Here is how to choose and apply a theme.",
"## Start from the wedding itself",
"The best palettes come from the event: the bride's main saree or gown, the groom's outfit, the mandap or stage decor and the venue. Pick two or three dominant colours from a few key photos. In Photoshop, the Eyedropper tool can sample colours directly from images; save them as swatches.",
"## Build a simple palette",
"- **One main colour:** used for backgrounds or large areas (for example ivory, maroon or deep green).",
"- **One accent colour:** used for ornaments, borders and headings (often gold).",
"- **One neutral:** for text and calm areas (cream, white, charcoal).",
"Use the palette on every spread. You can vary the shade slightly between events while keeping the same family of colours.",
"## Classic Indian wedding palettes",
"- Maroon, gold and ivory: traditional and royal.",
"- Deep green, gold and cream: suits temple settings and South Indian weddings.",
"- Kasavu cream and gold: understated Kerala style.",
"- Pastel pink, mint and champagne: modern mehendi and day events.",
"- Navy, silver and white: evening receptions.",
"These are common choices, not rules; the photos should decide.",
"## Different events, related colours",
"Multi-day weddings often have very different outfits: yellow for haldi, green for mehendi, red for the ceremony, a gown or suit for the reception. Instead of forcing one palette everywhere, give each event its own variation while keeping the same neutral and the same accent colour. Gold or ivory accents can tie together very different event colours.",
"## Recolouring templates",
"Templates rarely match a couple's colours exactly. Add a Hue/Saturation or Color Balance adjustment layer and clip it to the ornament or background (Alt+Ctrl+G). Shift the hue to your palette and lower saturation for a refined look. Gradient Map adjustment layers can turn a texture into any two-colour combination. These edits are non-destructive and easy to reuse across spreads.",
"## Keep skin tones natural",
"Strong coloured backgrounds can make skin look off by contrast. A bright green background beside warm skin, for example, can make faces look redder. If faces look wrong next to the background, lower the background's saturation or choose a more neutral shade.",
"## Text colour",
"Use your neutral or accent colour for text. Gold text on a light background can be hard to read; add a subtle shadow or choose a darker gold. Keep text colour consistent throughout the album.",
"## Test the palette",
"Before designing the full album, make two or three spreads with the palette and view them side by side at a small size. If they feel connected, continue; if not, adjust before you have thirty spreads to change.",
"## Templates by colour",
"Our [golden album PSD tag](/tag/golden-album-psd/), [floral album PSDs](/tag/floral-album-psd/) and [album background collection](/album-background-psd/) are good starting points for building a consistent palette. Pair this guide with [choosing the right album background](/blog/choose-album-background-psd/)."]),
})
_ADD5={
'does-photoshop-have-album-templates':"Whichever source you use, keep one master copy of every template untouched and work on duplicates. That way a mistaken merge or flatten never destroys a layout you rely on, and you can always return to the clean version for the next client.",
'album-design-software-options':"Whatever you choose, test it on one real album before committing for a whole season. Time how long a full album takes from culling to export, note where you get stuck and compare the printed result. That small trial tells you more than any feature list.",
'what-is-dm-album-psd':"Finally, remember that names vary between regions and sellers. You may see the same kind of sheet described as a DM design, a Karizma sheet, a 12x36 album PSD or simply an album template. What matters is the canvas size, the resolution, whether the layers are editable and whether the style suits your client. Check those four things and the label stops mattering. When you share sheets with a lab or another designer, describe them by size and resolution rather than by a nickname, so nobody is confused about what you need.",
'album-design-freelance-guide':"Finally, keep a simple record of every project: the studio, album size, sheet count, turnaround and any feedback. Over a season this shows which clients are worth prioritising, how long different album types really take and where your process can be faster. That information makes pricing and scheduling far easier the following year, and it helps you say no politely to work that does not fit.",
}
for _k,_t in _ADD5.items():
    LONG[_k][1].append(_t)
